---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="A collaborative lab for AI safety."
  eyebrow="About"
  description="Akxar Labs is an open AI safety lab. We build clearer evidence around how advanced AI behaves — and we do it in the open, with collaborators."
>
  <section class="about-grid">
    <div>
      <div class="lab-stat">
        <strong>03</strong>
        <span>Research programs: alignment, evaluation, and human oversight.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="lab-stat" style="margin-top: 34px;">
        <strong>Open</strong>
        <span>Methods, tools, and results shared with the wider safety community.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="lab-stat" style="margin-top: 34px;">
        <strong>2026</strong>
        <span>Founded to make safety research a shared effort.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        We study the practical questions that sit between model capability and public benefit: when
        systems reason well, when they fail, and how people can stay meaningfully in control.
      </p>
      <p>
        We believe safety is a shared problem, so we work as a collaborative lab — publishing open
        problems, inviting visiting researchers, and partnering with other teams on evaluations and
        shared infrastructure.
      </p>
      <h2>How We Work</h2>
      <p>
        Our research combines empirical evaluation, prototype design, and public-facing explanation.
        Outputs include papers, reproducibility reports, open-source tools, and field notes from
        real deployments — all written so others can build on them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0;">
    <div class="values-grid">
      <article class="value-card">
        <h3>Evidence first</h3>
        <p>Claims should be testable, reproducible, and honest about uncertainty.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="value-card">
        <h3>Human agency</h3>
        <p>AI systems should make people more capable without hiding judgment or tradeoffs.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="value-card">
        <h3>Public clarity</h3>
        <p>Research should be written so technical and nontechnical audiences can act on it.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
